  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The graph between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>u</mi></mfrac></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>v</mi></mfrac></math> for a thin convex lens in order to determine its focal length is plotted as shown in the figure. The refractive index of lens&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;and its both the surfaces have same radius of curvatures <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> will be _____ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cm</mi></math>.</p><p>(Where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo></math> object distance, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo></math> image distance)</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/4789e12f-5151-4569-8ed1-2f4edd8182e7-image.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 299px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "10",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/4789e12f-5151-4569-8ed1-2f4edd8182e7-image.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 299px;\" /></p><p>For point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>u</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>v</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> Thus, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8734;</mo></math></p><p>Using lens formula,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>f</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>v</mi></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>u</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math></p><p>Now, using Lens maker&#39;s formula,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>f</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mn>1</mn></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mstyle></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>, where,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#956;</mi></math>&nbsp;is refractive index of lens.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math></p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
  },
